      "title": "Personal Income and Outlays, September 2026",
      "summary": "<p>Personal income increased $54.5 billion (0.2 percent at a monthly rate) in September, according to estimates released today by the U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA). Disposable personal income (DPI)&ndash;personal income less personal current taxes&ndash;increased $52.7 billion (0.2 percent), and personal consumption expenditures (PCE) increased $113.1 billion (0.5 percent). Personal outlays&ndash;the sum of PCE, personal interest payments, and personal current transfer payments&ndash;increased $113.0 billion in September. Personal saving was $911.1 billion, and the personal saving rate&ndash;personal saving as a percentage of DPI&ndash;was 3.8 percent.\n</p>",
